{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner, amending the scope of request d50ce26d (firm authority chain design) with two points from hugh's direction on 2026-10-02. (1) Rooms that hold collections of other Rooms (a service catalogue, a firm's roster) must never be a control plane in the command sense. The design must keep the rule that a Room's admission never reads another Room: anything a cell relies on from elsewhere is recorded in the cell's own log by digest before use, so the log stays replayable alone. The firm's mandate is therefore a signed object from the firm's own Room, carried into the cell and verified against the firm's key as pinned in the cell's roster when the firm joined, with no live dependency. The one cross-Room push the design may propose is revocation, delivered as a signed object and sealed by each cell as its own system entry. (2) R-ADM-3 case (b) requires the grantor to be an active member of the cell, and R-GEN-7 teams are sets of members, not keyholders, so the note must say how a firm becomes a keyholding principal in a cell, or propose the amendment that lets a team hold a key. Collection membership belongs in the registry keyed by genesis fields, never in a Room's log."}